From 91fca02958a218836fc31def1f538645e30e30f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:56:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(desktop): remember a backend that refuses
 prompt.submit's submission_id

hermes serve's tui_gateway contract has no submission_id and refuses it
pre-admission (4000). Desktop downgraded per submission, so EVERY message to
the hub paid a refused request plus the identityless resend: an extra
Mac->hub round trip (renderer trace: 6/6 test chats). Remember the refusal
per submission destination (connection + profile) for 10 min, and send
identityless straight away. An accepted identity clears it, and the entry
expires so an upgraded backend gets identity back. The safety rules are
unchanged: only a pre-admission refusal downgrades, and a lost identityless
ACK is never auto-retried.

Retained (explicit-retry) entries always offer their identity again: one may already
be admitted with identity, and dropping it would bypass dedupe. The memo is valid only in the
gateway activation epoch it was recorded in (a route/source swap can land on a capable
backend under the same key).

A refusal is stamped with the activation epoch its request was SENT under and dropped
if a swap happened while it was in flight.

Tests: new submission-identity-support unit tests. The legacy-identity tests
moved to their own file (index.test.tsx is over its line cap). The new
'remembers the refusal' test fails without the fix. The lost-ACK test's
count drops from 4 requests to 3, because the third send no longer pays the
refused request. A global afterEach resets the memo. Full use-prompt-actions
+ use-session-actions suites: 944/944. tsc: 0 desktop errors.
